<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venetian Ghetto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1516">1516</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Gheto de Venesia, Ghetto Nuovo, Ghetto Vecchio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Venetian Ghetto was the area of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>'s Cannaregio district in which the government of the Venetian Republic forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> to live, and the origin of the English word ghetto. A decree of Doge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonardo-loredan">Leonardo Loredan</a> and the Senate of 29 March 1516 ordered all Jews in the city into the Ghetto Nuovo, where they were locked in at night under Christian surveillance, paid rents a third higher than before and could not own property. Its German, Italian, Spanish and Portuguese and Levantine communities kept synagogues of their own. In 1797 the French army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> ended its separation from the city. It remains a centre of Venice's Jewish community of about 450 people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/venetian-ghetto.jpg" alt="Venetian Ghetto" width="330" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghetto_(Venice)_Panorama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the defeat at Agnadello in 1509 brought refugees from Vicenza and Conegliano and tensions with the Christians grew, the <b>Venetian Ghetto</b> was established on 29 March 1516 and enlarged in 1541 for the Levantine Jews.</blockquote><a href="/societies/venice">Social Hierarchy of the Republic of Venice</a></li></ul></section>
